        {
          "kicker": "New squad face",
          "heading": "Ulster's Jamie Benson, once in England A, now in Ireland's squad",
          "body": "Jamie Benson, a 24-year-old back who started out at Richmond in London, is now part of Andy Farrell's Ireland squad for the Nations Championship. His mother, Carole, grew up in Belfast, and Benson says he is very proud of his Irish heritage, though he initially set out to make his name with England. Farrell called him into training in July, before he had even joined Ulster from Harlequins, and the versatile back has impressed for his new province since."
