        {
          "kicker": "Squad depth",
          "heading": "Quesada says Italy identified 67 players of national interest at season start",
          "body": "Gonzalo Quesada has identified 67 players of national interest since the season began, all monitored physically and medically as well as technically. Some are close to the squad; others are long-term options. Italy open the November window against South Africa in Turin, then face Argentina in Genoa and Fiji in Udine before the final phase in London: four straight matches against top-ten opposition, a year out from the World Cup."
        },
        {
