          "kicker": "Australia A form",
          "heading": "McLaughlin-Phillips leads Australia A to 52-0 shutout of USA in New Jersey",
          "body": "Australia A completed a clean sweep of the USA Eagles with a 52-0 win in New Jersey, after a thumping opener in Nashville. Bledisloe Cup debutant Harry McLaughlin-Phillips led the way, scoring a try, setting up at least three more and piling on 17 points. Western Force back Mac Grealy, whom Wallabies coach Les Kiss name-dropped over the weekend, was one of several backs with five-pointers, while the forward trio of Nick Frost, Will Harris and Toby Macpherson dominated the USA lineout."
        },
