      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad versatility",
          "heading": "Leicester Fainga'anuku gives Dave Rennie hybrid bench options, Stephen Donald says",
          "body": "Leicester Fainga'anuku, named in the 36-man squad for the November matches after missing the July games and Rugby's Greatest Rivalry series, gives Rennie options across the back row and backs. Stephen Donald says the 27-year-old, who has mostly played centre or wing but started at openside in Super Rugby Pacific this year, could let New Zealand carry two loose forwards without burning a back reserve. It is expected he will feature against Scotland, with Rennie naming the side next week."
        },
